{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#257","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#257","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#257\",\"parent_revision\":\"f0517f9e2d9623b5922208336e599548421d6aaa\",\"root_revision\":\"67aa2636f6e88cfc461fea7b253e5b031796b18407d1eb043bd7402dad28813b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWrap `implementation_manager.py` CLI as MCP tools. Agents could query task status, list pending tasks, and update task state programmatically. Tools: `query_tasks`, `list_pending`, `update_task_status`, `parse_task_file`.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **development-harness: task status mcp** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: MCP backlog audit 2026-02-23\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested Location\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/mcp/server.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Implementer has verified `implementation_manager.py` exists and identifies its unique capabilities vs. the SAM MCP server\\n- [ ] Tool list is narrowed to only capabilities NOT already in the SAM server\\n- [ ] New MCP tools registered in `plugin.json` and accessible via `fastmcp list`\\n- [ ] Each tool has a typed input schema (no `Any` or `object` parameters)\\n- [ ] Round-trip test: agent calls tool, verifies state change, calls read-back tool to confirm\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n1. Does `implementation_manager.py` still exist in `plugins/development-harness/`? Or was it replaced by the SAM task system?\\n2. Which of the proposed tools (`query_tasks`, `list_pending`, `update_task_status`, `parse_task_file`) are not already covered by `sam_task`, `sam_plan`, and `sam_active_task` in the existing SAM MCP server?\\n3. Should this be a new separate MCP server, or additional tools added to the existing `run_backlog_server.py`?\\n4. Is this still a priority feature, or has the SAM server made it obsolete?\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\nFunctional intent: PRESENT \u2014 expose task state query and mutation as MCP tools so agents can check and update task status programmatically.\\n\\n**Available**:\\n- Existing SAM MCP server: `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` already provides `sam_task` (read/claim/update/state), `sam_plan` (read/create/list/status/ready/update), `sam_active_task` (get/set/update/clear)\\n- FastMCP 3.x + PEP 723 pattern established in the codebase\\n- `plugins/development-harness/mcp/` suggested as target location\\n\\n**Gap 1 \u2014 `implementation_manager.py` existence unverified**: The description says wrap this file as MCP tools, but it is unclear whether `implementation_manager.py` still exists in the codebase or has been superseded by the SAM task system. Must verify at work time.\\n\\n**Gap 2 \u2014 Overlap with SAM MCP server**: The proposed tools (`query_tasks`, `list_pending`, `update_task_status`, `parse_task_file`) overlap significantly with tools already in the SAM server. Item may be partially or fully superseded. Implementer must compare the SAM server's capability against the proposed tool list before building.\\n\\n**Gap 3 \u2014 Priority mismatch**: Item was added as priority `Ideas` (2026-02-23) but current labels show no priority. Confirm intended priority before committing effort.\\n\",\"digest\":\"6766bc868b3d955637c0fb203c8f18b839bfc3c7aa7219e0def2ba6cb03f0b9d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg13QQ\"}"}